-- ============================================================================
-- Memory Match — individual multiplayer memory game (game #17)
--
-- 2–4 players compete SOLO (no teams, no shared score). Players take turns
-- flipping two cards; a match earns 1 pair (+1 point) and another turn, a
-- miss flips the cards back and passes the turn. Matched cards are marked
-- with the winner's color/avatar instead of being removed, so everyone can
-- see who is leading. Game ends when all pairs are found.
--
-- DYNAMIC DIFFICULTY (auto mode, default):
--   2 players → 16 cards (4×4,  8 pairs)   ~1–2 min
--   3 players → 20 cards (5×4, 10 pairs)   ~2–3 min
--   4 players → 24 cards (6×4, 12 pairs)   ~3–5 min
-- Custom: easy 16 / medium 20 / hard 24 / expert 36 (6×6).
--
-- SERVER-AUTHORITATIVE (never trust the client):
--   • fn_memorymatch_flip validates: game running, caller IS the current
--     player, turn not expired, card in range, unmatched, unflipped, and
--     at most 2 flips per turn. FOR UPDATE row lock serializes flips.
--   • Match evaluation happens ONLY server-side (pair ids never leave the
--     server until both cards are revealed).
--   • fn_memorymatch_advance applies the reveal outcome only after the
--     timed reveal window; turns pass automatically when the 15 s timer
--     expires (fn_memorymatch_tick watchdog, run by every client).
--
-- TIE RULES (equal pairs): (1) found pairs faster (lower cumulative match
-- offset), (2) fewer wrong attempts, (3) earlier join.
-- ============================================================================

